{
  "slug": "east-maui-ditch-system-ownership-and-county-takeover-bid",
  "title": "East Maui ditch system ownership and county takeover bid",
  "summary": "As of September 18, 2026, there was nothing new to report on land negotiations for the East Maui irrigation system. On August 23, Board of Land and Natural Resources (BLNR) unanimously denied staff's recommendation to start a long-term water license for Mahi Pono, keeping alive the county's effort to take over management through the East Maui Water Authority. Ownership is disputed, since the last licenses expired between 1971 and 1986 and a state letter says the system is private.",
  "topics": [
    "water",
    "government"
  ],
  "status": "active",
  "pinned": false,
  "firstSeenISO": "2024-11-14",
  "lastSeenISO": "2026-09-18",
  "signals": {
    "meetingsLast30d": 1,
    "meetingsLast90d": 3,
    "mentionsLast30d": 1,
    "upcomingEvent": null
  },
  "asOfISO": "2026-10-16",
  "timeline": [
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-09-18",
      "text": "There was nothing new to report on land negotiations for the East Maui irrigation system.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "jggU3kzKFQI",
        "ts": "0:55:03",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:03:54.314Z"
      },
      "body": "Aha Moku o Maui Hikina"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "That price affects money owed to the Department of Hawaiian Homelands and the Office of Hawaiian Affairs.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "Yufg5sEmpnc",
        "ts": "0:21:54",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:09.149Z"
      }
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "The presenter said ownership changes how the state prices a water license, which affects money for the Department of Hawaiian Homelands and the Office of Hawaiian Affairs.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "Yufg5sEmpnc",
        "ts": "0:21:35",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:09.149Z"
      }
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "State staff cited the company's ownership of one ditch stretch as a reason to reject the county's request to take over the system.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "Yufg5sEmpnc",
        "ts": "0:15:18",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:09.149Z"
      }
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "The presenter said the company clearly owns only one stretch of the Wailoa ditch, which the county needs to reach a treatment plant.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "Yufg5sEmpnc",
        "ts": "0:14:39",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:09.149Z"
      }
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "The presenter said those licenses say the aqueducts become government property when the license ends.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "xpuBwsHeXRw",
        "ts": "0:13:46",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:08.282Z"
      }
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "Those licenses said the aqueduct system would revert to the government when they ended.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "Yufg5sEmpnc",
        "ts": "0:13:44",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:09.149Z"
      }
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "The last water licenses for the four license areas expired between 1971 and 1986.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "xpuBwsHeXRw",
        "ts": "0:13:06",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:08.282Z"
      }
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "The presenter said the state constitution holds all public natural resources in trust for the people.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "Yufg5sEmpnc",
        "ts": "0:10:55",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:09.149Z"
      }
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "Just over 24 million gallons a day came from state lands from January through November 2025.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "xpuBwsHeXRw",
        "ts": "0:10:30",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:08.282Z"
      }
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "The presenter said most of the system's water comes from state lands, not company lands.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "Yufg5sEmpnc",
        "ts": "0:10:12",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:09.149Z"
      }
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "A state land department letter said the system is privately owned, so the department cannot transfer it.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "Yufg5sEmpnc",
        "ts": "0:08:48",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:09.149Z"
      }
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "The vice chair said the vote keeps alive the county's effort, through the East Maui Water Authority, to take over management of the system.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "9vFQege7xis",
        "ts": "0:06:51",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:09.917Z"
      },
      "body": "East Maui Regional Community Board"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "Board of Land and Natural Resources (BLNR) voted to deny its staff's recommendation to start a long-term water license for Mahi Pono.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "9vFQege7xis",
        "ts": "0:06:43",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:09.917Z"
      },
      "body": "East Maui Regional Community Board"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "The presenter said the new owner is owned by a Canadian government pension investment board.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "xpuBwsHeXRw",
        "ts": "0:04:24",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:08.282Z"
      }
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "One key ditch section feeds the largest of the county's three East Maui surface water treatment plants.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "xpuBwsHeXRw",
        "ts": "0:03:31",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:08.282Z"
      }
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "There were about 8 hours of testimony, and oral testimony was about 95% opposed.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "9vFQege7xis",
        "ts": "0:02:12",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:09.917Z"
      },
      "body": "East Maui Regional Community Board"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "Staff instead recommended starting the process to issue a long-term water license to Mahi Pono.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "9vFQege7xis",
        "ts": "0:02:04",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:09.917Z"
      },
      "body": "East Maui Regional Community Board"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "Board of Land and Natural Resources (BLNR) staff concluded the county was not qualified to get a set aside of the assets and run the system.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "9vFQege7xis",
        "ts": "0:01:56",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:09.917Z"
      },
      "body": "East Maui Regional Community Board"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "In 2025, Alexander and Baldwin sold its full interest in the East Maui Irrigation Company.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "xpuBwsHeXRw",
        "ts": "0:01:13",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:08.282Z"
      }
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-23",
      "text": "A presenter described the East Maui irrigation system, mostly built between the 1870s and 1920s.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "Yufg5sEmpnc",
        "ts": "0:00:31",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:09.149Z"
      }
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-20",
      "text": "He said ownership of the ditch system matters because the state must price any license through an appraisal.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "UjHForbD6sQ",
        "ts": "0:39:45",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:10.862Z"
      },
      "body": "Board of Water Supply"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-08-20",
      "text": "In a presentation, he said most water in the system comes from state lands.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "UjHForbD6sQ",
        "ts": "0:28:52",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-07T23:26:10.862Z"
      },
      "body": "Board of Water Supply"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-05-15",
      "text": "Motion to enter executive session on negotiations of real property related to the irrigation system: The board voted to go into executive session on property negotiations.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "6QAT7xS4o6U",
        "ts": "1:20:07",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-09T06:35:05.182Z"
      },
      "body": "East Maui Regional Community Board"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-05-15",
      "text": "The board voted to go into executive session (a closed-door discussion) about property negotiations tied to the irrigation system.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "6QAT7xS4o6U",
        "ts": "1:19:38",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-09T06:35:05.182Z"
      },
      "body": "East Maui Regional Community Board"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-05-15",
      "text": "The chair said the state needs to know who owns the system, whether it licenses the system or sets it aside to the county.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "6QAT7xS4o6U",
        "ts": "0:35:14",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-09T06:35:05.182Z"
      },
      "body": "East Maui Regional Community Board"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-05-15",
      "text": "The chair said state deputy attorneys general have disagreed with the chair's ownership analysis.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "6QAT7xS4o6U",
        "ts": "0:20:14",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-09T06:35:05.182Z"
      },
      "body": "East Maui Regional Community Board"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-05-15",
      "text": "The chair said the last four state water licenses all expired between the 1970s and the 1980s.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "6QAT7xS4o6U",
        "ts": "0:16:08",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-09T06:35:05.182Z"
      },
      "body": "East Maui Regional Community Board"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2026-05-15",
      "text": "The mayor sent the state a letter saying the county is ready to take over the ditch system.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "6QAT7xS4o6U",
        "ts": "0:06:31",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-09T06:35:05.182Z"
      },
      "body": "East Maui Regional Community Board"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2024-12-12",
      "text": "The director said this state item is different from a long-term license.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "2obBIqFggos",
        "ts": "1:21:20",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-09T06:35:06.415Z"
      },
      "body": "East Maui Regional Community Board"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2024-12-12",
      "text": "The board discussed a state land board item on the East Maui irrigation system set for December 13, 2024.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "2obBIqFggos",
        "ts": "1:11:50",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-09T06:35:06.415Z"
      },
      "body": "East Maui Regional Community Board"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2024-11-21",
      "text": "The East Maui speaker said the mayor wants to bring all stakeholders together to discuss a new way to manage East Maui water.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "XD60_Qatcxw",
        "ts": "0:09:30",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-09T06:35:07.486Z"
      },
      "body": "Board of Water Supply"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2024-11-14",
      "text": "The director said the land board will probably want to hear results of talks in about six months.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "5iHkOVL1-vQ",
        "ts": "0:37:32",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-09T06:35:08.811Z"
      },
      "body": "East Maui Regional Community Board"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2024-11-14",
      "text": "The chair said five land board members voted for a motion to deny the proposal.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "5iHkOVL1-vQ",
        "ts": "0:36:26",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-09T06:35:08.811Z"
      },
      "body": "East Maui Regional Community Board"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2024-11-14",
      "text": "Over 200 pieces of testimony were submitted, and over 90% were opposed, the chair said.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "5iHkOVL1-vQ",
        "ts": "0:35:20",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-09T06:35:08.811Z"
      },
      "body": "East Maui Regional Community Board"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2024-11-14",
      "text": "The chair said the proposal would effectively close off the board's ability to move forward.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "5iHkOVL1-vQ",
        "ts": "0:34:03",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-09T06:35:08.811Z"
      },
      "body": "East Maui Regional Community Board"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2024-11-14",
      "text": "The chair said the board got no advance notice.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "5iHkOVL1-vQ",
        "ts": "0:32:42",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-09T06:35:08.811Z"
      },
      "body": "East Maui Regional Community Board"
    },
    {
      "dateISO": "2024-11-14",
      "text": "The chair said a long-term East Maui water license item returned to the state land board's agenda on November 1.",
      "basis": "said-at-meeting",
      "source": {
        "type": "meeting",
        "videoId": "5iHkOVL1-vQ",
        "ts": "0:31:50",
        "retrievedISO": "2026-10-09T06:35:08.811Z"
      },
      "body": "East Maui Regional Community Board"
    }
  ],
